        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Neutrophils are also capable of secreting GRO-alpha, IL-1beta, IL-1ra, IL-3, IL-12, IP-10, MIG, MIP-1alpha, MIP-1beta, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha, VEGF, and anti-microbial peptides. They can positively influence the chemotaxis of basophils, T-cells, monocytes, macrophages, dendritic cells, and other neutrophils. Neutrophils are also CD35-positive, CD64-positive, CD89-positive, CD184-positive, and fMLP receptor-positive Ly-6G-positive (mouse), TLR2-low, TLR4-low, and lineage-negative (CD2, CD3, CD5, CD9, CD19, CD36, CD49d, CD56, CD61, CD235a (glycophorin-A)).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">mature neutrophil</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">neutrophil (normally intravascular only)</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
