        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic interneuron marked by Lamp5 and Lhx6 expression, derived from the Medial Ganglionic Eminence (MGE), and located in the pallium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A transcriptomically distinct lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Lamp5 and Lhx6. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: &apos;Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization&apos;, dataset: &apos;Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons&apos;, Author Categories: &apos;CrossArea_subclass&apos;, Lamp5 Lhx6.</obo:IAO_0000115>
