        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A capillary tuft which forms a close network with the visceral epithelium (podocytes) and the mesangium to form the filtration barrier and is surrounded by Bowman&apos;s capsule in nephrons of the vertebrate kidney[GO].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ZFA - The multi-tissue structure where the glomerular basement membrane supported by mesonephric podocytes filters blood from the glomerular capillaries. GUDMAP: &apos;Together, the Bowman&apos;s capsule and the glomerulus comprise the definitive renal corpuscle.&apos; - here the glomerulus is part of the capsule?</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
