        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">One of the four structures within the heart that prevent backflow of blood by opening and closing with each heartbeat. The valves include two semilunar valves, the aortic and pulmonary; the mitral or bicuspid valve; and the tricuspid valve. The valves permit blood flow in only one direction. [TFD][VHOG]</owl:annotatedTarget>
