        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The biceps femoris is a muscle of the posterior (the back) thigh. As its name implies, it has two parts, one of which (the long head) forms part of the hamstrings muscle group. [WP,unvetted].</owl:annotatedTarget>
