        <obo:UBPROP_0000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In some types, the cuneiform is found as two or three bones, in which case the more anterior (&apos;dorsal&apos; in dorsal/plantar terminology) is the ectocuneiform, while the more posterior or plantar bones are the mesocuneiform and entocuneiform.[Palaeos]</obo:UBPROP_0000005>
