        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The opaque muscular contractile diaphragm suspended in the aqueous humour in front of the lens of the eye. The organ is perforated by the pupil and continues peripherally with the ciliary body. [Dorian_AF, Elsevier&apos;s_encyclopaedic_dictionary_of_medicine, Part_B:_Anatomy_(1988)_Amsterdam_etc.:_Elsevier][VHOG]</owl:annotatedTarget>
