        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Vascular layer containing connective tissue, of the eye lying between the retina and the sclera. The choroid provides oxygen and nourishment to the outer layers of the retina. Along with the ciliary body and iris, the choroid forms the uveal tract[WP].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">check choroid vs choroid layer; check ZFA/TAO placement - no homology assertion in VHOG. Note this is entirely in the posterior region of eyeball in ZFA</obo:IAO_0000116>
