        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The layer of polyhedral cells in the epidermis found between the stratum granulosum and stratum basale; shrinkage and adhesion of these cells gives a spiny or prickly appearance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Has cells that produce and secrete bipolar lipids which prevent evaporation, helping to &apos;water-proof&apos; the skin. Keratinization begins in the stratum spinosum. [Wikipedia:Stratum_spinosum]</obo:UBPROP_0000009>
