    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002116">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002108"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The portion of the small intestine that extends from the jejunum to the colon.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TODO consider ZFA:0000706 posterior intestine, see also colon</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Although all vertebrates have a digestive tract and accessory glands, various parts of this system are not necessarily homologous, analogous, or even present in all species. Therefore, broad comparisons can be best made under the listings of headgut, foregut, midgut, pancreas and biliary system, hindgut.[uncertain][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ileal</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The ileum is the final section of the small intestine in most higher vertebrates, including mammals, reptiles, and birds. In fish, the divisions of the small intestine are not as clear and the terms posterior intestine or distal intestine may be used instead of ileum.[Wikipedia:Ileum]</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AAO:0010403</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
