        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Tonsils on the left and right sides at the back of the throat. one of the mucosa-associated lymphoid tissues (MALT), located at the entrance to the upper respiratory and gastrointestinal tracts to protect the body from the entry of exogenous material through mucosal sites[WP].</obo:IAO_0000115>
