            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A mucous membrane that lines the mouth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">this is defined as any mucous membrane of the mouth - including palate, lips, uvula, etc. ncit split mouth/oral mucosa into lip and buccal. In future we may split into masticatory/keratinized (gingiva + hard palate) vs lining/non-keratinized (lips, cheeks, floor of mouth, soft palate). FMA distinguishes between mucosa of mouth and region of mouth (the latter including the buccal mucosa)</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the mucous membrane epithelium of the mouth. It can be divided into three categories: masticatory, lining, and specialized[Wikipedia:Oral_mucosa].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
