        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A three-dimensional arrangement formed by plates of hepatocytes, usually one cell thick, that radiates from the center of the liver lobule; hepatic laminae are highly branched, irregular structures bordered by endothelial lined vascular spaces called hepatic sinusoids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
