        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The orbicularis oris is a superficial facial muscle with fibers that encircle the opening of the oral cavity that attaches to the maxilla, mandible, skin and modiolus, and that participates in oral/pharyngeal behaviors, and is innervated by the facial nerve (CN VII).</obo:IAO_0000115>
