        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The anterior digastric is a pharyngeal arch I muscle that participates in oral/pharygeal behaviors and is innervated by the nerve to mylohyoid and superficial to mylohyoid muscle, and lacks the midline raphe.[FEED]</owl:annotatedTarget>
