        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The slit-like opening of either ureter into the bladder; normally, the two ureteral orifices are placed at the posterolateral angles of the urinary bladder trigone while the internal urethral orifice is placed at its anteroinferior angle (apex); wide gaping usually indicates vesicoureteral reflux.</obo:IAO_0000115>
