        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A corkscrew-like artery in premenstrual or progestational endometrium; uterine spiral arteries play a vital role in supplying nutrients to the placenta and fetus, and are thus remodeled into highly dilated inelastic vessels by the action of invading trophoblast (physiological change).</obo:IAO_0000115>
