        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A long slender branch of the anterior inferior cerebellar artery (85%-100% cases) or basilar artery (&lt;15% cases), arises from near the middle of the artery; it accompanies the vestibulocochlear nerve through the internal acoustic meatus, and is distributed to the internal ear.</obo:IAO_0000115>
